        "revision": 1301191618,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "R. aureum is widely cultivated as an ornamental plant, in traditional, native plant, drought tolerant, and wildlife gardens, and natural landscaping projects. Named cultivars have been also introduced.\nAlthough the flowers are hermaphroditic, the yield is greatly benefited by cross-pollination.",
